From 6b75e232c900c8c6aede9651fc8d276defa2ce54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:00:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): event order ignores a backfilled uid's clock
 [daveey]

`kanban_sync_divergence._event_order` (also the terminal guard's
`terminal_hold` order) ordered same-second events by any UUIDv7 uid's
milliseconds. `kanban_db_sync` backfills uid-less rows with a v7 stamped
at backfill time, so a backfilled row sorted last in its second instead
of falling back to arrival (local id) order, and could misorder a
terminal vs reopen event of that second.

It now routes through `consistent_uid_milliseconds(uid, created_at)`
(PR #3010): a uid is trusted only when its ms fall in the row's own
second, else the ms key is created_at*1000 and the id decides, the same
rule `kanban_shared_blockers._event_order` uses.

Follow-up from review of PR #3010 (review 5905718508, nit 1);
card t_01a1dad6b27ce69d.

Proof:
- RED on fa6ec16e2e: the new terminal_hold tests (backfilled uid on the
  earlier-id completed/reopened event, both kinds) and the
  _event_order unit tests fail (4 failed).
- GREEN: every tests/hermes_cli file importing kanban_sync_divergence,
  kanban_terminal_guard or kanban_shared_blocker*: 37 files, 930 passed.
- Replay over this worker's real boards (798 DBs, read-only, 17,386
  tasks): terminal_hold result changed for 0 tasks; 126,019 v7 uids sit
  outside their row's second and are now ignored for ordering.
- scripts/check --only health: ok.
